; Grass — TerrainDefinition data entry (spec.md -> Data Schemas; terrain.md ->
; Already-Defined Terrain, v1 tag-source mapping).
;
; emitted_tags = ["open_grass"] is DECIDED (terrain.md's tag-source mapping, Open Question
; #5 closed -> D-25). No radius, no weight, no threshold: a tile emits its terrain's tags
; and nothing else.
;
; cost = 0 is terrain.md's one pricing rule — "nature is free; construction costs
; materials" — a decided design rule rather than a tuning number.
;
; MODEL_SCENE NOW POINTS AT REAL ART: GrassCommonShort.tscn (CC0, MegaKit), chosen over
; GrassCommonTall as the default because "short" reads as the more generic ground-cover
; pick for a tile that is meant to be the default open-grass floor, not an accent; Tall
; remains imported and available at
; project/assets/terrain/grass_common_tall/GrassCommonTall.tscn for a future per-tile
; variety pass (out of scope here — no random-variant scattering logic added). Scale is
; still the FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL recorded in GrassCommonShort.tscn's own header comment
; (raw mesh scaled to ~0.15 tile-units, judgment call, no GDD number) — NOT eyeball-
; confirmed in-engine; that confirmation is a human call, not this repo's to make.
;
; SLAB REINSTATED (2026-08-03) in GrassCommonShort.tscn: TerrainView._refresh_tile_visual()
; instantiates model_scene as a tile's ENTIRE visual, and the bare grass-tuft prop alone
; left most of the tile showing scenes/Main.tscn's configured WorldEnvironment sky-blue
; background_color (0.53, 0.72, 0.86) straight through the gap — reported by an in-engine
; human look as "completely transparent, just blue." Fixed by reinstating a ground slab
; matching the grey-box placeholder's geometry and color verbatim. See
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's own header for detail. Prop-on-slab look still awaits full
; human sign-off.
;
; SCATTERED CLUSTER (2026-08-03): a follow-up human look reported the single tuft-on-slab
; as looking wrong ("a single tuft," "quite funny"); GrassCommonShort.tscn now hand-places
; 6 varied instances of the same imported mesh instead of one, to read as coverage — see
; that scene's header for the transforms. Still awaits full human sign-off.
;
; MODEL_SCENE PLURALIZED TO MODEL_SCENES (-> D-42): the field is now an array so a
; terrain can carry multiple interchangeable visual variants, stably picked per tile by
; TerrainDefinition.pick_variant().
;
; LOOK-PASS REWORK (2026-08-16): GrassCommonTall is now wired as a second live variant
; alongside GrassCommonShort — human complaint was "needs to actually look like grass
; across the whole tile, rather than just a few sprigs." Both scenes were reworked first
; (denser scatter, blotchy floor patches — see each .tscn's own header) so either variant a
; tile lands on reads as full-tile grass coverage, not just the previously-live Short. No
; new grass mesh source was pulled in for THIS wiring (Tall was already imported and
; unused, same D-42 opportunity as Forest's CommonTree2) — see this pass's other terrain
; entries (Rock, Cultivated field) for where genuinely new sources were needed instead.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TerrainDefinition" load_steps=4 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/terrain_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/grass_common_short/GrassCommonShort.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/grass_common_tall/GrassCommonTall.tscn" id="3_model"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "grass"
display_name = "Grass"
emitted_tags = Array[String](["open_grass"])
cost = 0
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model"), ExtResource("3_model")])
harvestable = null
